Blocks contract: kind=blocks. on maps each distinct block name to a support block or TABLE. TABLE is reserved, supports must exist, and self-support, cycles, or more than one block directly on a block are malformed. TABLE may support several blocks. goal_on is a partial map using existing blocks or TABLE; self-support, cycles, and multiple blocks directly assigned to one block are contradictory and malformed. The initial state and goals here are well-formed. A block is clear when no block is directly on it. plan is an ordered list of {block,to} actions. A move is legal exactly when block exists and is clear, to is TABLE or an existing clear block distinct from block, and to differs from block's current support. A legal move changes only that block's support. At the first illegal move, include its {legal:false,after:unchanged_on_map} step, stop immediately, and ignore subsequent moves. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed move was legal. reaches_goal means the entire plan is valid and every goal_on entry equals the final on-map entry; unspecified supports need not change. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL on-map that satisfies every goal_on entry, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the complete sequence of (block,to) string pairs. It is [] when the initial state already satisfies the goal and null if unreachable. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:on_map}], after:on_map, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.
